    "rich_text_x7rw9D": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_pR3cPK": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "Keep your truffle soil in the narrow zone where truffles can actually thrive",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_Vzw6X3": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>Truffles are famously picky about their soil. pH, iron, potassium, salinity, texture, organic matter, and even the balance of key trace elements such as boron and zinc all influence whether and how well the truffle fungus can colonize roots and produce fruit. Unlike climate, soil chemistry and many soil properties can and do change more quickly over time—with irrigation, amendments, and weather. </p><p>ATC's Soil Analysis Service is designed specifically for Périgord black truffle orchards. It gives you a clear, repeatable picture of your soil each year, so you can maintain it within the narrow window required for successful Périgord black truffle cultivation and avoid slow, silent drift away from optimal conditions. </p>"
          }
        },
        "button_NbrY8X": {
          "type": "button",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "button_primary_label": "Other Services",
            "button_primary_style": "primary",
            "button_primary_link": "shopify://pages/our-technology",
            "button_secondary_label": "Let's Begin",
            "button_secondary_style": "secondary",
            "button_secondary_link": "shopify://pages/contact"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_pR3cPK",
        "description_Vzw6X3",
        "button_NbrY8X"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich_text.name",
