    "image_with_text_wriCk3": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_QjgYaD": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "Turn soil trends into better management and yield potential",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_NLUUwd": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>The real power of annual soil analysis is in the trend line. When you monitor soil every year—and combine that information with root analysis and orchard performance—you can see how management decisions are actually affecting the underground environment. Because of our scientific approach, ATC is a strong proponent of regular testing for soil, trees, and truffle fungus; our monitoring experience and global data sets allow us to interpret your soil data in a truffle-specific context and advise you on any corrective measures required.</p>"
          }
        },
        "subheading_iffgpk": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading_text": "Over time, this lets you:"
          }
        },
        "description_wPtnnp": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<ul><li>Confirm that changes in irrigation, amendments, or groundcover are moving conditions in the right direction.</li><li>Anticipate potential yield issues years in advance, rather than reacting after poor seasons.</li><li>Align your soil management with benchmarks drawn from productive truffle orchards in regions with similar climates and/or soil conditions.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
